      32 !-----------------------------------------------
      33 !
      34 !     *
      35 !     THIS SUBROUTINE ATTEMPTS TO MINIMIZE A REAL-VALUED FUNCTION OF
      36 !     THE N-COMPONENT REAL VECTOR XPARAM ACCORDING TO THE
      37 !     BFGS FORMULA. RELEVANT REFERENCES ARE
      38 !
      39 !     BROYDEN, C.G., JOURNAL OF THE INSTITUTE FOR MATHEMATICS AND
      40 !                     APPLICATIONS, VOL. 6 PP 222-231, 1970.
      41 !     FLETCHER, R., COMPUTER JOURNAL, VOL. 13, PP 317-322, 1970.
      42 !
      43 !
      44 !     SHANNO, D.F. MATHEMATICS OF COMPUTATION, VOL. 24, PP 647-656
      45 !                    1970.
      46 !
 
 FORCHECK PC V13.5.13          FLEPO           2021-03-24 10:59:30   page:  3444
 flepo.F90  /FF
 
      47 !   SEE ALSO SUMMARY IN
      48 !
      49 !    HEAD, J.D.; AND ZERNER, M.C., CHEMICAL PHYSICS LETTERS, VOL. 122,
      50 !          264 (1985).
      51 !    SHANNO, D.F., J. OF OPTIMIZATION THEORY AND APPLICATIONS
      52 !          VOL.46, NO 1 PP 87-94 1985.
      53 !     *
      54 !     THE FUNCTION CAN ALSO BE MINIMIZED USING THE
      55 !     DAVIDON-FLETCHER-POWELL ALGORITHM (COMPUTER JOURNAL, VOL. 6,
      56 !     P. 163).
      57 !
      58 !     THE USER MUST SUPPLY THE SUBROUTINE
      59 !     COMPFG(XPARAM,.TRUE.,FUNCT,.TRUE.,GRAD,LGRAD)
      60 !     WHICH COMPUTES FUNCTION VALUES  FUNCT AT GIVEN VALUES FOR THE
      61 !     VARIABLES XPARAM, AND THE GRADIENT GRAD IF LGRAD=.TRUE.
      62 !     THE MINIMIZATION PROCEEDS BY A SEQUENCE OF ONE-DIMENSIONAL
      63 !     MINIMIZATIONS.  THESE ARE CARRIED OUT WITHOUT GRADIENT COMPUTATIO
 N
      64 !     BY THE SUBROUTINE LINMIN, WHICH SOLVES THE SUBPROBLEM OF
      65 !     MINIMIZING THE FUNCTION FUNCT ALONG THE LINE XPARAM+ALPHA*PVECT,
      66 !     WHERE XPARAM
      67 !     IS THE VECTOR OF CURRENT VARIABLE VALUES,  ALPHA IS A SCALAR
      68 !     VARIABLE, AND  PVECT  IS A SEARCH-DIRECTION VECTOR PROVIDED BY TH
 E
      69 !     BFGS OR DAVIDON-FLETCHER-POWELL ALGORITHM.  EACH ITERATION STEP C
 A
      70 !     OUT BY FLEPO PROCEEDS BY LETTING LINMIN FIND A VALUE FOR ALPHA
      71 !     WHICH MINIMIZES  FUNCT  ALONG  XPARAM+ALPHA*PVECT, BY
      72 !     UPDATING THE VECTOR  XPARAM  BY THE AMOUNT ALPHA*PVECT, AND
      73 !     FINALLY BY GENERATING A NEW VECTOR  PVECT.  UNDER
      74 !     CERTAIN RESTRICTIONS (POWELL, J.INST.MATHS.APPLICS.(1971),
      75 !     V.7,21-36)  A SEQUENCE OF FUNCT VALUES CONVERGING TO SOME
      76 !     LOCAL MINIMUM VALUE AND A SEQUENCE OF
      77 !     XPARAM VECTORS CONVERGING TO THE CORRESPONDING MINIMUM POINT
      78 !     ARE PRODUCED.
      79 !                          CONVERGENCE TESTS.
      80 !
      81 !     HERBERTS TEST: THE ESTIMATED DISTANCE FROM THE CURRENT POINT
      82 !                    POINT TO THE MINIMUM IS LESS THAN TOLERA.
      83 !
      84 !                    "HERBERTS TEST SATISFIED - GEOMETRY OPTIMIZED"
      85 !
      86 !     GRADIENT TEST: THE GRADIENT NORM HAS BECOME LESS THAN TOLERG
      87 !                    TIMES THE SQUARE ROOT OF THE NUMBER OF VARIABLES.
      88 !
      89 !                    "TEST ON GRADIENT SATISFIED".
      90 !
      91 !     XPARAM TEST:  THE RELATIVE CHANGE IN XPARAM, MEASURED BY ITS NORM
 ,
      92 !                   OVER ANY TWO SUCCESSIVE ITERATION STEPS DROPS BELOW
      93 !                   TOLERX.
      94 !
      95 !                    "TEST ON XPARAM SATISFIED".
      96 !
      97 !     FUNCTION TEST: THE CALCULATED VALUE OF THE HEAT OF FORMATION
      98 !                    BETWEEN ANY TWO CYCLES IS WITHIN TOLERF OF
      99 !                    EACH OTHER.
     100 !
     101 !                    "HEAT OF FORMATION TEST SATISFIED"
 
 FORCHECK PC V13.5.13          FLEPO           2021-03-24 10:59:30   page:  3445
 flepo.F90  /FF
 
     102 !
     103 !     FOR THE GRADIENT, FUNCTION, AND XPARAM TESTS A FURTHER CONDITION,
     104 !     THAT NO INDIVIDUAL COMPONENT OF THE GRADIENT IS GREATER
     105 !     THAN TOLERG, MUST BE SATISFIED, IN WHICH CASE THE
     106 !     CALCULATION EXITS WITH THE MESSAGE
     107 !
     108 !                     "PETERS TEST SATISFIED"
     109 !
     110 !     WILL BE PRINTED, AND FUNCT AND XPARAM WILL CONTAIN THE LAST
     111 !     FUNCTION VALUE CUM VARIABLE VALUES REACHED.
     112 !
     113 !
     114 !     ALGORITHMS CHOOSE SEARCH DIRECTIONS
     115 !     ON THE BASIS OF LOCAL PROPERTIES OF THE FUNCTION.  A MATRIX  H,
     116 !     WHICH IN FLEPO IS PRESET WITH THE IDENTITY, IS MAINTAINED AND
     117 !     UPDATED AT EACH ITERATION STEP.  THE MATRIX DESCRIBES A LOCAL
     118 !     METRIC ON THE SURFACE OF FUNCTION VALUES ABOVE THE POINT XPARAM.
     119 !     THE SEARCH-DIRECTION VECTOR  PVECT  IS SIMPLY A TRANSFORMATION
     120 !     OF THE GRADIENT  GRAD  BY THE MATRIX H.
