     722 !-----------------------------------------------
     723 !**********************************************************************
 *
     724 !
     725 !    PLATO  is part of the SYMMETRY package.  It generates the
     726 !           unitary transform which will orientate the system
     727 !           so that the 'Z' axis is an axis of rotation.
     728 !
     729 !    PLATO is called when the system belongs to a cubic point group.
     730 !          Atoms nearest to the center of symmetry are identified.
     731 !          If there are 4, 6, 8, 12, or 20, then they outline one
     732 !          of the Platonic solids (tetrahedron, octahedron, cube,
     733 !          icosahedron, or pentagonal dodecahedron).  In that case,
     734 !          each atom lies on a 3, 4, or 5 fold symmetry axis.
     735 !
     736 !          In other cases the axis of symmetry lies goes through a
     737 !          regular polygon, either an equilateral triangle, a square,
     738 !          or a regular pentagon.
     739 !
     740 !          The unitary transform is returned through R.
     741 !
     742 !**********************************************************************
 
